    "name": "harness",
    "description": "Show the Herdr-Jev harness plan and workers in a pane; /harness review runs the harness review",
    "output": "Harness pane opened. No plan yet: the advisor starts one with harness_plan."
   }
  ],
  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "harness_plan",
    "description": "Plan an objective as bounded tasks. Herdr-Jev assigns each task a role and the models come from herdr-jev models list (reader or mechanic for small work, implementer for code, advisor for architectural work); implementer and mechanic tasks get an independent review by the reviewer from Herdr-Jev. When the AI Harness delegation plan returns a consult stage for the complexity of a task, a read-only consultant runs first and that task waits for you: read its recommendation with harness_status, then decide and start it with harness_run taskId. Returns the plan with stable task ids. Main session only."
   },
   {
    "name": "harness_run",
    "description": "Start harness workers as background subagents. With taskId, run that task (an advisor task is marked done instead). Without it, run every proposed task whose dependencies are done and that has no consult, up to the worker limit. Safe to call twice: a running task returns its existing agent id. Main session only."
   },
   {
    "name": "harness_status",
    "description": "Text summary of the harness plan, workers, open questions and last review."
   },
   {
    "name": "harness_collect",
    "description": "Collect the recorded automatic run. Explicit verify=true can start its original queued implementation if it has never been claimed, or run checks and independent review after it returns. Never creates a replacement run. Main session only."
   },
   {
    "name": "harness_delegate",
    "description": "After reading a completed automatic consult in harness_status, accept its recommendation and start the shared execution plan, or pass accept=false to decline and continue directly. Main session only."
   }
  ],
